{
	quest.B100000000000258.title: "Osmium Supply"
	quest.B100000000000258.quest_subtitle: "Mekanism · Materials"
	quest.B100000000000258.quest_desc: [
		"&6Goal:&r Smelt &616 Osmium Ingots&r.",
		"",
		"Osmium is Mekanism's core metal — circuits, machines, compressors, and alloys all burn through it.",
		"",
		"&6How:&r\n&e1.&r Mine &6Osmium Ore&r (or raw osmium) from the world.\n&e2.&r Smelt ore/raw into &6Osmium Ingots&r in any furnace, or enrich first for double dust yield.",
		"",
		"&7Tip:&r Create crushers work for early ore lines if your Mekanism hall is not up yet.",
		"",
		"&7Next:&r Stock iron and carbon — steel infusion is next.",
		"",
		"&6Connected:&r",
		"{\"text\":\"\\u2192 Brass Age\",\"color\":\"yellow\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"B1000000000000DF\"}}"
	]
	quest.B100000000000259.title: "Steel Infusion"
	quest.B100000000000259.quest_subtitle: "Mekanism · Materials"
	quest.B100000000000259.quest_desc: [
		"&6Goal:&r Craft &616 Steel Ingots&r.",
		"",
		"Steel unlocks &6Steel Casings&r — the chassis under nearly every Mekanism machine.",
		"",
		"&6How:&r\n&e1.&r Place a &6Metallurgic Infuser&r and power it (Energy Cube, cable, or charged Energy Tablet).\n&e2.&r Put &6Coal&r, &6Charcoal&r, or &6Enriched Carbon&r in the infusion extra slot.\n&e3.&r Insert &6Iron Ingots&r; collect &6Steel Ingots&r from the output (or pull steel from IE/MI if you already make it elsewhere).",
		"",
		"&7Tip:&r Enrich coal in an Enrichment Chamber later — enriched carbon lasts far longer than raw fuel.",
		"",
		"&7Next:&r Batch steel into Steel Casings."
	]
	quest.B10000000000025A.title: "Steel Casing"
	quest.B10000000000025A.quest_subtitle: "Mekanism · Foundation"
	quest.B10000000000025A.quest_desc: [
		"&6Goal:&r Craft &68 Steel Casings&r.",
		"",
		"Almost every Mekanism machine sits on a Steel Casing. Batch them before the machine rush.",
		"",
		"&6How:&r\n&e1.&r Craft casings from &6Steel&r, &6Osmium&r, and &6Glass&r (check JEI for the exact pattern).\n&e2.&r Keep a stack ready — Enrichment Chamber, Crusher, Factories, and Energy Cubes all consume them.",
		"",
		"&7Tip:&r Pair casings with Basic Control Circuits for the first machine wave.",
		"",
		"&7Next:&r Make Basic Control Circuits next."
	]
	quest.B10000000000025B.title: "Basic Circuits"
	quest.B10000000000025B.quest_subtitle: "Mekanism · Foundation"
	quest.B10000000000025B.quest_desc: [
		"&6Goal:&r Craft &68 Basic Control Circuits&r.",
		"",
		"Circuits gate every machine tier. Basic is the first stop; Advanced/Elite/Ultimate climb the alloy ladder.",
		"",
		"&6How:&r\n&e1.&r Enrich &6Redstone&r in an Enrichment Chamber (or craft circuits once you have the recipe unlocked).\n&e2.&r In a &6Metallurgic Infuser&r, infuse &6Osmium Ingots&r with &6Enriched Redstone&r to form Basic Control Circuits.\n&e3.&r Stockpile — cables, transporters, and early machines each want several.",
		"",
		"&7Tip:&r Automate redstone enrichment before you mass-produce Advanced circuits.",
		"",
		"&7Next:&r Build a dedicated Metallurgic Infuser for the alloy line."
	]
	quest.B10000000000025C.title: "Metallurgic Infuser"
	quest.B10000000000025C.quest_subtitle: "Mekanism · Machines"
	quest.B10000000000025C.quest_desc: [
		"&6Goal:&r Craft a Metallurgic Infuser.",
		"",
		"The Infuser is the heart of Mekanism — steel, circuits, infused/reinforced/atomic alloys, and enriched materials all start here.",
		"",
		"&6How:&r\n&e1.&r Craft and place the Infuser; connect FE via &6Universal Cable&r or an &6Energy Cube&r.\n&e2.&r Open the GUI: main slot for the metal, left/extra slot for the infusion material (carbon, redstone, diamond, refined obsidian, tin, etc.).\n&e3.&r Use a &6Configurator&r (Shift+right-click) to set auto-eject and side modes so pipes can pull outputs.\n&e4.&r Optional: enrich materials first (coal→enriched carbon, redstone→enriched redstone) so each bar lasts longer.",
		"",
		"&7Tip:&r Energy Tablets charge early machines before your cable network is ready.",
		"",
		"&7Next:&r Add an Enrichment Chamber for 2× ore dust and enriched infusion stock."
	]
	quest.B10000000000025D.title: "Enrichment Chamber"
	quest.B10000000000025D.quest_subtitle: "Mekanism · Machines"
	quest.B10000000000025D.quest_desc: [
		"&6Goal:&r Craft an Enrichment Chamber.",
		"",
		"Tier-1 ore processing: enrich ore → dust → smelt for double ingots. Also makes enriched redstone/diamond/carbon for the Infuser.",
		"",
		"&6How:&r\n&e1.&r Place and power the chamber; pipe ores into the input with Logistical Transporters or hoppers.\n&e2.&r Enrich raw ores/ores into dusts, then smelt dusts for ~2× yield versus raw smelting.\n&e3.&r Enrich redstone, diamond, coal, and refined-obsidian inputs for Metallurgic Infuser bars.\n&e4.&r Configurator: enable auto-eject and lock sides so dusts leave cleanly into a furnace line.",
		"",
		"&7Tip:&r Speed and energy upgrades pay for themselves once ore lines are feeding it.",
		"",
		"&7Next:&r Add a Crusher for dirt/dust intermediates and factory upgrades later."
	]
	quest.B10000000000025E.title: "Mekanism Crusher"
	quest.B10000000000025E.quest_subtitle: "Mekanism · Machines"
	quest.B10000000000025E.quest_desc: [
		"&6Goal:&r Craft a Mekanism Crusher.",
		"",
		"Crushers turn clumps, shards, and crystals into dirty dusts/dusts along the higher ore-processing tiers — and crush solids for FE-powered dust lines.",
		"",
		"&6How:&r\n&e1.&r Place next to your Enrichment Chamber and power both.\n&e2.&r Basic line: Enrich ore → smelt. Better line: Purification/Injection products → Crusher → Enrichment → Furnace.\n&e3.&r Set side config so crushed outputs feed the Enrichment Chamber automatically.",
		"",
		"&7Tip:&r A Basic Tier Installer turns this into a multi-slot factory later.",
		"",
		"&7Next:&r Infuse iron with redstone for Infused Alloy."
	]
	quest.B10000000000025F.title: "Infused Alloy"
	quest.B10000000000025F.quest_subtitle: "Mekanism · Alloys"
	quest.B10000000000025F.quest_desc: [
		"&6Goal:&r Craft &68 Infused Alloys&r.",
		"",
		"Redstone-infused iron is the first alloy tier — Advanced circuits, mid machines, and transporters need it.",
		"",
		"&6How:&r\n&e1.&r In the Metallurgic Infuser, load &6Enriched Redstone&r (or redstone) as the infusion type.\n&e2.&r Insert &6Iron Ingots&r; collect &6Infused Alloy&r from the output.",
		"",
		"&7Tip:&r Keep a dedicated Infuser on redstone so you are not constantly swapping carbon/redstone/diamond bars.",
		"",
		"&7Next:&r Craft Advanced Control Circuits."
	]
	quest.B100000000000260.title: "Advanced Circuits"
	quest.B100000000000260.quest_subtitle: "Mekanism · Alloys"
	quest.B100000000000260.quest_desc: [
		"&6Goal:&r Craft &64 Advanced Control Circuits&r.",
		"",
		"Advanced circuits unlock Purification, Injection, Osmium Compressor, Digital Miner, and factory installers.",
		"",
		"&6How:&r\n&e1.&r Craft Advanced Control Circuits from &6Basic Control Circuits&r + &6Infused Alloy&r (JEI).\n&e2.&r Stockpile extras — every upgrade path burns through these.",
		"",
		"&7Tip:&r Automate infused alloy before chasing Elite circuits (reinforced alloy + advanced circuit).",
		"",
		"&7Next:&r Build the Purification Chamber for the next ore-yield jump."
	]
	quest.B100000000000261.title: "Purification Chamber"
	quest.B100000000000261.quest_subtitle: "Mekanism · Ore processing"
	quest.B100000000000261.quest_desc: [
		"&6Goal:&r Craft a Purification Chamber.",
		"",
		"Oxygen-assisted purification is the next yield tier after enrichment — ores become clumps that crush into more dust.",
		"",
		"&6How:&r\n&e1.&r Place and power the Purification Chamber.\n&e2.&r Pipe &6Oxygen&r in via &6Pressurized Tubes&r from an Electrolytic Separator (or Chemical Tank).\n&e3.&r Feed ores; clumps leave the item output — crush → enrich → smelt for the upgraded chain.\n&e4.&r Configurator: chemical input on one side, items on others; enable auto-eject.",
		"",
		"&7Tip:&r One separator can feed multiple purification machines if oxygen is buffered in a chemical tank.",
		"",
		"&7Next:&r Build the Electrolytic Separator for O₂/H₂."
	]
	quest.B100000000000262.title: "Electrolytic Separator"
	quest.B100000000000262.quest_subtitle: "Mekanism · Gases"
	quest.B100000000000262.quest_desc: [
		"&6Goal:&r Craft an Electrolytic Separator.",
		"",
		"Splits water into &6Hydrogen&r and &6Oxygen&r — purification, HCl, gas-burning power, and many chemical recipes depend on it.",
		"",
		"&6How:&r\n&e1.&r Place and power the Separator; pipe &6Water&r into the fluid input (sink, pump, or Create hose).\n&e2.&r Connect &6Pressurized Tubes&r from the O₂ and H₂ sides to tanks or machines.\n&e3.&r Configurator: set dump modes if one gas backs up and stalls the machine (common when only oxygen is used).\n&e4.&r Store surplus hydrogen in a Chemical Tank or burn it in a Gas-Burning Generator.",
		"",
		"&cCaution:&r If either gas output is full and dump is off, electrolysis stops — always give both gases somewhere to go.",
		"",
		"&7Tip:&r Salt → brine electrolysis later yields chlorine for Hydrogen Chloride.",
		"",
		"&7Next:&r Chemical Injection Chamber for elite ore yields."
	]
	quest.B100000000000263.title: "Chemical Injection"
	quest.B100000000000263.quest_subtitle: "Mekanism · Ore processing"
	quest.B100000000000263.quest_desc: [
		"&6Goal:&r Craft a Chemical Injection Chamber.",
		"",
		"Hydrogen Chloride injection pushes ore processing into elite shard yields — the step before full slurry/crystal lines.",
		"",
		"&6How:&r\n&e1.&r Make &6Hydrogen Chloride&r: Chemical Infuser combining &6Hydrogen&r + &6Chlorine&r (chlorine from brine in an Electrolytic Separator).\n&e2.&r Pipe HCl into the Injection Chamber via Pressurized Tubes; power the machine.\n&e3.&r Feed ores → shards; crush shards → dirty dust → enrich → smelt.\n&e4.&r Later (optional): Chemical Dissolution + Sulfuric Acid → slurry → Chemical Washer → Crystalizer for max yield.",
		"",
		"&7Tip:&r Buffer HCl in a Basic Chemical Tank so the chamber never starves mid-batch.",
		"",
		"&7Next:&r Osmium Compressor for refined glowstone/obsidian products."
	]
	quest.B100000000000264.title: "Osmium Compressor"
	quest.B100000000000264.quest_subtitle: "Mekanism · Machines"
	quest.B100000000000264.quest_desc: [
		"&6Goal:&r Craft an Osmium Compressor.",
		"",
		"Compresses liquid osmium onto dusts for refined glowstone, refined obsidian, and other late intermediates on the Atomic Alloy path.",
		"",
		"&6How:&r\n&e1.&r Place and power the compressor; feed it &6Osmium&r (ingots/blocks as the recipe requires — check JEI).\n&e2.&r Insert the dust/material to compress; collect refined products from the output.\n&e3.&r Pipe inputs with Logistical Transporters; keep a chest of osmium beside it.",
		"",
		"&7Tip:&r Pair with a Combiner when recipes want compressed blocks or blended dusts.",
		"",
		"&7Next:&r Climb to Atomic Alloy once reinforced alloy and refined obsidian are flowing."
	]
	quest.B100000000000265.title: "Universal Cables"
	quest.B100000000000265.quest_subtitle: "Mekanism · Logistics"
	quest.B100000000000265.quest_desc: [
		"&6Goal:&r Craft &632 Basic Universal Cables&r.",
		"",
		"Universal Cables move FE between cubes, machines, chargepads, and generators — Mekanism's power bus.",
		"",
		"&6How:&r\n&e1.&r Craft a stack of &6Basic Universal Cables&r and place them like redstone dust between machines.\n&e2.&r Connect an &6Energy Cube&r or generator on one end and your machine cluster on the other.\n&e3.&r Sneak-Configurator on a cable connection to set pull/push if energy is not flowing the way you expect.",
		"",
		"&7Tip:&r Upgrade cable tiers when transfer rate stalls under factory load.",
		"",
		"&7Next:&r Add Logistical Transporters for items."
	]
	quest.B100000000000266.title: "Logistical Transporters"
	quest.B100000000000266.quest_subtitle: "Mekanism · Logistics"
	quest.B100000000000266.quest_desc: [
		"&6Goal:&r Craft &632 Basic Logistical Transporters&r.",
		"",
		"Mekanism item pipes with filters, color coding, and round-robin — excellent beside Create belts.",
		"",
		"&6How:&r\n&e1.&r Place transporters between inventories/machines like pipes.\n&e2.&r Use a Configurator to set pull on the source chest and push toward machines.\n&e3.&r Shift-Configurator cycles color; matching colors keep ore lines from mixing.\n&e4.&r Add Logistical Sorters later for filtered routing into multiple machines.",
		"",
		"&7Tip:&r Round-robin helps feed multi-slot factories evenly.",
		"",
		"&7Next:&r Pressurized Tubes for chemicals and gases."
	]
	quest.B100000000000267.title: "Pressurized Tubes"
	quest.B100000000000267.quest_subtitle: "Mekanism · Logistics"
	quest.B100000000000267.quest_desc: [
		"&6Goal:&r Craft &616 Basic Pressurized Tubes&r.",
		"",
		"Move chemicals and gases between separators, chambers, tanks, and injectors without buckets.",
		"",
		"&6How:&r\n&e1.&r Place tubes from Electrolytic Separator outputs to Purification / Injection / Chemical Tanks.\n&e2.&r Configurator on tube ends sets pull/push; mismatched modes are the usual 'no gas flowing' bug.\n&e3.&r Buffer expensive gases in Chemical Tanks so machines do not stall mid-craft.",
		"",
		"&7Tip:&r Keep radioactive or expensive gases on dedicated color-coded networks.",
		"",
		"&7Next:&r Park an Energy Cube at the center of the machine hall."
	]
	quest.B100000000000268.title: "Energy Cube"
	quest.B100000000000268.quest_subtitle: "Mekanism · Power"
	quest.B100000000000268.quest_desc: [
		"&6Goal:&r Craft a Basic Energy Cube.",
		"",
		"Cubes buffer FE for machine halls so generators can keep working through demand spikes.",
		"",
		"&6How:&r\n&e1.&r Place the cube centrally among machines; cable generators into input sides.\n&e2.&r Configurator each face: input from power, output toward machines (or use Universal Cables freely).\n&e3.&r Upgrade Advanced → Elite → Ultimate as Digital Miner and factories demand more buffer.",
		"",
		"&7Tip:&r Short cable runs from a central cube cut transfer bottlenecks.",
		"",
		"&7Next:&r QIO storage once power is stable — or Tier Installers for factories."
	]
	quest.B100000000000269.title: "Factory Installer"
	quest.B100000000000269.quest_subtitle: "Mekanism · Factories"
	quest.B100000000000269.quest_desc: [
		"&6Goal:&r Craft a Basic Tier Installer.",
		"",
		"Right-click a machine to turn it into a Factory with more parallel processing slots — huge ore-line throughput.",
		"",
		"&6How:&r\n&e1.&r Craft a &6Basic Tier Installer&r (Advanced circuits + alloys — check JEI).\n&e2.&r Right-click a placed Enrichment Chamber, Crusher, Infuser, etc. to convert it into a Basic Factory.\n&e3.&r Higher installers (Advanced/Elite/Ultimate) upgrade the same machine further in place.\n&e4.&r Re-pipe items after upgrading — slot counts and side configs can need a refresh.",
		"",
		"&7Tip:&r Plan floor space; factories are wider in the GUI and hungry for power.",
		"",
		"&7Next:&r Digital Miner when you want filter-based area mining."
	]
	quest.B10000000000026A.title: "Digital Miner"
	quest.B10000000000026A.quest_subtitle: "Mekanism · Late tools"
	quest.B10000000000026A.quest_desc: [
		"&6Goal:&r Craft a Digital Miner.",
		"",
		"Filter-based area mining that pulls ores (and more) without you swinging a pick — the ultimate ore vacuum.",
		"",
		"&6How:&r\n&e1.&r Place the miner with clear space; connect serious FE (Energy Cube + upgraded cables).\n&e2.&r Open the GUI: set radius, Y min/max, silk touch / fortune modes as desired.\n&e3.&r Add item filters for the ores you want (or inverse-filter junk).\n&e4.&r Start the miner; pull items out with Logistical Transporters into storage.",
		"",
		"&cCaution:&r A wide unfiltered miner will shred the landscape and lag the area — set filters before starting.",
		"",
		"&7Tip:&r Anchor it near a QIO or RS system so ores never sit in the internal buffer.",
		"",
		"&7Next:&r Atomic Disassembler for a configurable all-tool."
	]
	quest.B10000000000026B.title: "Atomic Disassembler"
	quest.B10000000000026B.quest_subtitle: "Mekanism · Late tools"
	quest.B10000000000026B.quest_desc: [
		"&6Goal:&r Craft an Atomic Disassembler.",
		"",
		"A configurable all-tool that scales with energy — mining, combat, vein, and slow modes in one charged package.",
		"",
		"&6How:&r\n&e1.&r Craft the Disassembler (Atomic Alloy and late components — JEI).\n&e2.&r Charge it on a &6Chargepad&r wired to your energy network, or in an Energy Cube GUI.\n&e3.&r Sneak-scroll or use the mode key to switch digging/vein/slow modes as needed.",
		"",
		"&7Tip:&r Energy upgrades and a full cube make vein mode feel instant.",
		"",
		"&7Next:&r QIO Dashboard for wireless bulk storage."
	]
	quest.B10000000000026C.title: "QIO Dashboard"
	quest.B10000000000026C.quest_subtitle: "Mekanism · Storage"
	quest.B10000000000026C.quest_desc: [
		"&6Goal:&r Craft a QIO Dashboard.",
		"",
		"Quantum Item Orchestration stores huge item volumes wirelessly once drives and frequencies are linked.",
		"",
		"&6How:&r\n&e1.&r Craft a &6QIO Drive Array&r, insert &6QIO Drives&r, and set a frequency name.\n&e2.&r Craft the &6QIO Dashboard&r and set it to the same frequency.\n&e3.&r Place QIO Exporters/Importers on chests or machine I/O to move items on that frequency.\n&e4.&r Expand with larger drives as ore lines fill the first drive.",
		"",
		"&7Tip:&r One frequency per base keeps things simple until you need isolation.",
		"",
		"&7Next:&r Atomic Alloy for teleporters and elite crafts."
	]
	quest.B10000000000026D.title: "Atomic Alloy"
	quest.B10000000000026D.quest_subtitle: "Mekanism · Endgame"
	quest.B10000000000026D.quest_desc: [
		"&6Goal:&r Craft &64 Atomic Alloys&r.",
		"",
		"Diamond-then-obsidian infused alloy is Mekanism's top crafting tier for teleporters, elite machines, and MekaSuit modules.",
		"",
		"&6How:&r\n&e1.&r Infuse &6Infused Alloy&r with diamond → &6Reinforced Alloy&r.\n&e2.&r Make &6Refined Obsidian Dust&r (Enrich obsidian → compress with osmium as recipes require).\n&e3.&r Infuse Reinforced Alloy with refined obsidian → &6Atomic Alloy&r.",
		"",
		"&7Tip:&r Automate the full alloy ladder before chasing MekaSuit modules.",
		"",
		"&7Next:&r Frame a Mekanism Teleporter."
	]
	quest.B10000000000026E.title: "Mekanism Teleporter"
	quest.B10000000000026E.quest_subtitle: "Mekanism · Endgame"
	quest.B10000000000026E.quest_desc: [
		"&6Goal:&r Craft a Mekanism Teleporter.",
		"",
		"Linked portals give instant base-to-base travel once frames and frequencies are set.",
		"",
		"&6How:&r\n&e1.&r Build a portal frame from &6Teleporter Frame&r blocks (usually a hollow rectangle like a nether portal).\n&e2.&r Place the &6Teleporter&r block in the frame; power it heavily.\n&e3.&r Set matching frequencies on two teleporters; walk in to travel.\n&e4.&r Buffer FE in an Energy Cube beside each pad — jumps are energy-hungry.",
		"",
		"&7Tip:&r Frames are cheap; energy cost and correct frequency linking are the real setup.",
		"",
		"&7Next:&r Chapter complete — push factories, ore tiers, and QIO as your base grows."
	]
}
